Z||000000||HummelHund||04-17-2001||12:10 PM||||I just recieved the Yokohama Avid T4 215/60TR14's I ordered from the Tire Rack ($227 total!). Has anyone else put these tires on their Fiero? How did they perform? It was pretty hard to find 215/60R14's, which is what my car came with orignially (according to the RPO codes), but the good reviews and low price of the Yokohamas won me over.<P>Sean<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6||||reg||5
Z||000001||ChadMan||04-17-2001||12:39 PM||||I just got two Firehawk SS20's from the Tire Rack in 215/60R14 and am not completely happy with them.  They're great in the rain and they ride nicely, but seem to have a very soft sidewall and "squirm" a lot...I don't remember the Firehawk SS's on my old SE doing that.<P>Keep us posted on how you like the AVID's...I will keep them in mind the next time I need tires.||||reg||9
Z||000002||Oreif||04-17-2001||01:02 PM||||I only use BFGoodrich tires. On my lowered 86 SE I have 225/50HR15 Euro T/A's. Very strong sidewalls, excellent grip.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierojunky||04-17-2001||01:22 PM||||I have always ran Firestone Firehawks on my car - Now the SS20's i found that i had to air them up alitte to get them to ride right. ||||reg||1
